 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Erythrocytes, red blood cells, most abundant of all the cells. Adult man on an average has five to five point five millions of RBCs per cubic milliliter. Are these formed in the red bone marrow. Nucleus devoid in most mammals. Biconcave in shape. Hemoglobin, iron-containing complex protein. Red colored, hence the color, hence the name hemoglobin. Gram, three hundred ml, twelve to sixteen. Transport of respiratory gases. Lifespan, one hundred twenty days. Destroyed in spleen, graveyard of RBC. Hemoglobin, iron-containing complex protein. Red colored, hence the color, hence the name. Erythrocytes, red blood cells, most abundant of all the cells.",
