  "text": "Erythrocytes, red blood cells, most abundant of all the cells. Adult man on an average has 5 to 5.5 millions of RBCs per cubic millimeter. These. Found in the red bone marrow, nucleus, devoid in most mammals, by concave in shape. Hemoglobin, iron-containing complex protein, colored hence the color, hence the name. Hemoglobin, 300 ml, 12 to 16. Rich source of respiratory gases. Lifespan, 120 days, destroyed in spleen, graveyard of R. D. C. Hemoglobin, iron-containing complex protein, red color, hence the color, hence the name. Erythrocytes, red blood cells, most abundant of all the cells.",
